{"id":"manicom-rtw","title":"Sam Manicom: eight years round the world","who":"Sam Manicom","when":"1992–2000","vehicle":"BMW R80 GS","kind":"moto","color":"#be185d","media":[{"kind":"book","title":"Into Africa","by":"Sam Manicom"},{"kind":"book","title":"Under Asian Skies","by":"Sam Manicom","isbn":"9780955657306"},{"kind":"book","title":"Distant Suns","by":"Sam Manicom"},{"kind":"book","title":"Tortillas to Totems","by":"Sam Manicom"}],"summary":"He had ridden for three months when he left to cross Africa; he came back eight years and some 200,000 miles later, after 55 countries. Into Africa covers the Sahara to the Namib; Under Asian Skies runs from a container ship to Australia up through Southeast Asia and India and home via Iran and Turkey. Distant Suns (South America) and Tortillas to Totems (Mexico to North America) finish the story; those two are not mapped yet.","sources":[{"label":"Mad or Nomad: Sam Manicom, 8 lessons from 8 years","url":"https://www.madornomad.com/sam-manicom-8-lessons-from-8-years-on-the-road/"},{"label":"webBikeWorld: Into Africa & Under Asian Skies review","url":"https://www.webbikeworld.com/into-africa-under-asian-skies/"},{"label":"Wanderlust Journal: interview","url":"https://wanderlust-journal.com/2019/08/22/an-interview-with-sam-manicom/"}],"approximate":"Only the regions named in reviews of the first two books; the order and roads in between are unknown.","km":39625,"bbox":[-0.1278,-56.4847,151.2083,51.5074],"stops":[{"name":"England","place":"London, UK","at":[51.5074,-0.1278],"date":"1992","text":"Leaves with very little riding experience, for \"a year in Africa\".","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg/500px-London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg","page":"London","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Sahara","place":"Tamanrasset, Algeria","at":[22